WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.420
This chapter asks a specific question: A system can satisfy pre-deployment

2
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:10.780
requirements yet fail after release through drift, dependency failure, operator overload,

3
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:16.140
ambiguous incidents, correlated faults, or recovery actions that create new hazards.

4
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.035
The tempting shortcut is insufficient: Monitoring, a kill switch, backups,

5
00:00:21.035 --> 00:00:25.591
an incident plan, or rollback alone is not operational resilience:

6
00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:29.235
signals may be stale, effects may be irreversible,

7
00:00:29.235 --> 00:00:33.335
authority may be unclear, dependencies may share failure modes,

8
00:00:33.675 --> 00:00:38.375
and rollback may restore code while leaving data, memory, credentials,

9
00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:40.255
or downstream consequences changed.

10
00:00:40.855 --> 00:00:46.141
The chapter's core claim is this: Governed operation is a closed

11
00:00:46.141 --> 00:00:51.427
incident lifecycle that binds detection, classification, command authority, containment, effect-complete rollback,

12
00:00:51.427 --> 00:00:56.713
graceful degradation, recovery evidence, and learning to the exact deployed system

13
00:00:56.713 --> 00:00:58.635
and its dependency graph.

14
00:00:58.975 --> 00:01:04.530
Maintain a deployment manifest covering model, policy, prompts, tools, data, identities,

15
00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:10.085
caches, dependencies, owners, and rollback authority. Fuse behavioral, safety, security, dependency,

16
00:01:10.085 --> 00:01:15.640
human, and business signals into versioned incident hypotheses rather than a

17
00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.155
single health score.

18
00:01:17.495 --> 00:01:23.650
Classify incidents by consequence, reversibility, scope, uncertainty, and propagation risk.

19
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:28.280
A concrete implementation trace makes the proposal testable.

20
00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:33.945
Operate a fault-injected reference service with an exact deployment manifest,

21
00:01:33.945 --> 00:01:39.270
independent telemetry, a versioned incident workflow record, named incident roles,

22
00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:45.128
tool and credential revocation, safe degraded modes, full-state rollback plus external-effect

23
00:01:45.128 --> 00:01:46.725
compensation, staged recovery,

24
00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:51.387
and game-day scenarios including detector loss, correlated dependency failure,

25
00:01:51.387 --> 00:01:56.670
and a rollback that appears successful while hidden state remains changed.

26
00:01:56.670 --> 00:02:01.953
Fuse behavioral, safety, security, dependency, human, and business signals into versioned

27
00:02:01.953 --> 00:02:05.795
incident hypotheses rather than a single health score.

28
00:02:06.135 --> 00:02:11.368
Classify incidents by consequence, reversibility, scope, uncertainty, and propagation risk.

29
00:02:11.368 --> 00:02:16.602
Bind each class to incident commander, technical and safety leads,

30
00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:20.265
communication duties, action limits, and emergency expiry.

31
00:02:20.865 --> 00:02:25.782
The design can still fail. silent drift detector blindness alert storm

32
00:02:25.782 --> 00:02:30.700
ambiguous command The correct response is to stop, narrow, quarantine, compensate,

33
00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:35.170
or retain an owned residual rather than narrate uncertainty away.

34
00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:40.816
This chapter remains Design rationale at argument support. Its contracts, examples,

35
00:02:40.816 --> 00:02:44.945
tests, or local artifacts establish only their encoded scope.

36
00:02:44.945 --> 00:02:49.991
The chapter names proof targets rather than pretending they are already

37
00:02:49.991 --> 00:02:50.450
closed.

38
00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:56.622
Every finite degraded-mode transition preserves or narrows capability, data, tool,

39
00:02:56.622 --> 00:03:03.038
and duration authority. Normal-service recovery is rejected when any required internal-state

40
00:03:03.038 --> 00:03:08.870
component, external-effect disposition, acceptance check, or emergency-authority expiry is missing.

41
00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:13.540
Containment does not require the suspected component to cooperate.

42
00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:19.104
No chapter claim or evidence state is promoted by this visual.

43
00:03:19.104 --> 00:03:24.068
A named mechanism is not proof of correct implementation or useful

44
00:03:24.068 --> 00:03:29.032
